{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scaleUnits","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"by","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"factor","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Number","preciseIdentifier":"s:12XestiNumbers6NumberV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"anchor","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BeatTime","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/BeatTime","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTiming8BeatTimeV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"factor","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The factor to multiply each unit by.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"anchor","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The beat time from which units are scaled.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/UsingIvorTiming"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this after augmenting or diminishing the music from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":" by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"factor"},{"type":"text","text":", to keep its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound: each tempo keeps its rate, and its speed in whole notes per minute scales with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"music. For example, ♪ = 240 becomes ♩ = 240 when the music is augmented by 2."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":" changes speed. Unless "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":" is zero, an unscaled entry is first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inserted at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":", holding the tempo the music reaches there (the end of any ramp that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs into it). It comes before any entry already at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":", so the speed steps there."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Then every other entry at or after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":" has its unit scaled. If no entry was at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":", a scaled entry holding the tempo in effect there is inserted as well. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"includes "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/TempoMap\/defaultTempo","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", when this tempo map is empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inserting an entry inside a ramp splits it. The first part keeps its exact shape; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second becomes a fresh ease-in from the speed at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchor"},{"type":"text","text":" to the ramp’s end, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"close to the original but not identical."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"factor"},{"text":" is a positive rational number.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Multiplies the unit of every tempo from a beat time onward by a factor, keeping each rate."}],"identifier":{"url":"